{"schema":"LAW_EN_DOCUMENT_V1","id":"i18n-6a9309d7749dc0cd9866e2b72a885295efbfc86d288fc461","family_id":"KR:013220","country":"KR","language":"en","title":"ENFORCEMENT DECREE OF THE ACT ON MANAGEMENT OF FIREFIGHTING EQUIPMENT","title_original":"소방장비관리법 시행령","kind":"대통령령","source_version":"287377","promulgated":null,"effective":null,"translation_status":"AI_DRAFT","body_status":"BODY_LOADED","source_url":"https://www.law.go.kr/LSW/lsInfoP.do?lsiSeq=287377","source_sha256":"5ec8ed6d9986beb9b06e27df3fdfd117ffbb23733f907e5568d570449f38d7fc","body_sha256":"a1c2adea6b8d18b74bf24041062bab15f8c49ae19a0fb164c42e6abb3f6525d2","article_count":1,"full_text":"Article 33 (Operation of Fire Equipment) (1) “Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree” in Article 29 (2) 6 of the Act means any of the following:\n  1. Disaster preparedness drills pursuant to Article 35 of the Framework Act on the Management of Disasters and Safety;\n  2. Emergency duty pursuant to Article 5 of the Fire Officials Service Regulations;\n  3. Education and training of operator of fire equipment pursuant to Article 30 of the Act;\n  4. Inspection of fire equipment pursuant to Article 33 of the Act;\n  5. Maintenance of fire equipment pursuant to Article 35 of the Act.\n  (2) The operator of fire equipment shall report to the head of the competent fire service agency in advance before operating fire engines: Provided, That he or she need not report in any of the following cases:\n  1. Where it falls under subparagraphs 2 through 4 of Article 29 (2) of the Act;\n  2. Where it falls under subparagraph 1 or 2 of paragraph (1).","metadata":{"author_checks":["All current held source unit text, source editorial notes, amounts, periods, exceptions and source omission boundaries compared.","Unchanged official English retained only in the recorded exact source/target spans; original row, role, provider, edition, links and receipts remain unchanged.","New affected units are MACHINE_TRANSLATION / UNREVIEWED; source grap